                  'options': ['Increasing resistance to nuclease-mediated degradation, allowing ASOs to remain stable in biological environments for longer', 'Enhancing RNA-binding affinity through chemical modifications, allowing ASOs to bind more strongly to complementary target sequences', 'Improving endosomal escape following cellular uptake, allowing ASOs to reach intracellular RNA targets more efficiently', 'Enabling direct cleavage of target RNA without requiring recruitment of cellular enzymes such as RNase H'],
                  'correctIndex': 0,
                  'explanation': 'Replacing a backbone oxygen with sulfur (phosphorothioate) prevents exonucleases from recognising and degrading the ASO, extending its half-life from minutes to days compared with an unmodified oligonucleotide.',
                  'hashtags': ['Gene Therapy'],
                  'contributorName': 'Valerie',
                  'contributorEmail': 'vfrancessutanta@gmail.com',
