                  'explanation': 'Large, anionic siRNA molecules are rapidly filtered by the kidneys, cannot passively cross cell membranes, and are vulnerable to degradation in endosomes if they do get taken up — together giving unmodified siRNA very poor drug-like bioavailability.',
