              'mechanism': 'EC50 is the concentration producing half the maximal response and needs a functional assay, whereas Kd comes from binding and applies to agonists and antagonists. EC50 is not the same as Kd because of receptor number (spare receptors allow a maximal response without full occupancy), desensitisation, competing ligands and amplification in transduction pathways. On a log axis, curves are sigmoidal and easy to compare: a curve further left is more potent, and a lower plateau means lower efficacy. Organ-bath curves can be built by bolus dosing with a wash after each dose, or cumulatively by adding increasing concentrations without washing. Concentration conversions (e.g. 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ M = 100 pM = 0.1 nM) are needed to read curves.',
