                  'correctIndex': 1,
                  'explanation': 'Ammonium chloride acidifies urine; the base becomes BH⁺, which cannot diffuse back, so excretion rises. Acid un-ionises acids, not bases; filtration is unaffected by urinary pH; bicarbonate alkalinises urine, keeping the base un-ionised and reabsorbable.',
                  'difficulty': 'hard',
